Description: eventcomm.h: build the evdev (eventcomm) backend off Linux.
 <linux/version.h> is Linux-only; elsewhere the BUS_* macros of
 <linux/input.h> are undefined instead, as they clash with the server's
 BusType enum. NextBSD's <linux/input.h> is the base's <dev/evdev/input.h>
 (linux-input-shim). eventcomm is turned on by BUILD_EVENTCOMM=yes, as the
 port does. Unchanged from the port.
Origin: FreeBSD ports, x11-drivers/xlibre-xf86-input-synaptics/files/patch-src_eventcomm.h
 (https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-ports/blob/efd79beed9576dd3e354f889a41dabd5890921f4/x11-drivers/xlibre-xf86-input-synaptics/files/patch-src_eventcomm.h)
Forwarded: not yet; a candidate for X11Libre (FreeBSD support)
---
diff -ruN a/src/eventcomm.h b/src/eventcomm.h
--- a/src/eventcomm.h
+++ b/src/eventcomm.h
@@ -30,7 +30,15 @@
 #include <xorg-server.h>
 
 #include <linux/input.h>
+#ifdef __linux__
 #include <linux/version.h>
+#else
+#undef BUS_NONE
+#undef BUS_PCI
+#undef BUS_SBUS
+#undef BUS_PLATFORM
+#undef BUS_last
+#endif
 #include <xf86Xinput.h>
 #include "synproto.h"
 
